WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.814
Can one country exit the

2
00:00:01.814 --> 00:00:03.770
Indus Waters Treaty by itself?

3
00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.057
Signed in 1960, it gives

4
00:00:06.057 --> 00:00:07.918
India the eastern rivers:

5
00:00:08.068 --> 00:00:10.863
the Sutlej, the Beas and the Ravi.

6
00:00:11.163 --> 00:00:13.147
Pakistan, the western rivers:

7
00:00:13.297 --> 00:00:14.956
the Indus, the Jhelum and

8
00:00:14.956 --> 00:00:15.686
the Chenab.

9
00:00:16.186 --> 00:00:17.895
Under Article XII, it can

10
00:00:17.895 --> 00:00:19.194
be changed or ended

11
00:00:19.314 --> 00:00:21.397
only by a new treaty, ratified

12
00:00:21.397 --> 00:00:22.578
for that purpose.

13
00:00:23.128 --> 00:00:25.480
On 23 April 2025, India said

14
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.496
it would hold the treaty

15
00:00:27.496 --> 00:00:28.504
in abeyance,

16
00:00:28.624 --> 00:00:30.679
until Pakistan abjures support

17
00:00:30.679 --> 00:00:32.528
for cross-border terrorism.

18
00:00:32.978 --> 00:00:34.641
The next day, Pakistan said

19
00:00:34.641 --> 00:00:36.304
the treaty has no provision

20
00:00:36.304 --> 00:00:37.906
for unilateral suspension.

21
00:00:38.406 --> 00:00:40.646
On 31 August 2026, a Court

22
00:00:40.646 --> 00:00:42.714
of Arbitration held that

23
00:00:42.714 --> 00:00:45.126
the treaty remains in force.

24
00:00:45.376 --> 00:00:47.211
India rejected the award.

25
00:00:47.711 --> 00:00:48.777
One text.

26
00:00:49.077 --> 00:00:50.251
Two positions.

27
00:00:50.851 --> 00:00:51.789
Your turn.

28
00:00:52.089 --> 00:00:53.425
Which rivers go to India

29
00:00:53.425 --> 00:00:54.372
under the treaty?
